From: OpenWrt
Subject: [PATCH] clk: qcom: ipq6018: enable the source PLL across the NSS
 crypto RCG switch

nss_crypto_clk_src is reparented onto NSS_CRYPTO_PLL by the ppe node's
assigned-clock-rates, and that reparent happens from
of_clk_set_defaults() during the qca_ppe platform probe - i.e. before
any consumer has enabled the branch, so before anything has walked the
tree and enabled nss_crypto_pll{,_main}.

gcc_ipq6018_probe() only calls clk_alpha_pll_configure() on
nss_crypto_pll_main: that programs the PLL's config registers but does
not turn it on. An RCG's CMD_UPDATE bit only self-clears once the newly
selected source is actually running, so the switch times out after the
500us poll and the driver splats:

  nss_crypto_clk_src: rcg didn't update its configuration.
  WARNING: CPU: 3 PID: 1 at drivers/clk/qcom/clk-rcg2.c:136
  ...
  clk_rcg2_configure+0x88
  clk_rcg2_set_rate_and_parent+0x2c
  clk_change_rate+0x7c
  clk_core_set_rate_nolock+0x164
  clk_set_rate+0x38
  of_clk_set_defaults+0x69c
  platform_probe+0x38
  ...
  qca_ppe_driver_init+0x1c

leaving the RCG's CFG register pointing at a source it never latched,
which is what the NSS firmware's crypto block then runs off.

CLK_OPS_PARENT_ENABLE is the clock framework's answer to exactly this:
it makes clk_change_rate()/__clk_set_parent_before() prepare+enable both
the old and the new parent around the rate/parent change and drop them
again afterwards, so the PLL is spinning while the RCG latches. It is
the same flag other qcom controllers carry on RCGs whose parents are
gated at switch time.

Signed-off-by: Vladyslav Andreichykov <vladdrako007@gmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-ipq6018.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-ipq6018.c
@@ -1214,6 +1214,13 @@ static struct clk_rcg2 blsp1_qup1_i2c_ap
 		.name = "blsp1_qup1_i2c_apps_clk_src",
 		.parent_data = gcc_xo_gpll0_gpll0_out_main_div2,
 		.num_parents = 3,
+		/*
+		 * The reparent onto NSS_CRYPTO_PLL runs from
+		 * of_clk_set_defaults(), before any consumer has enabled
+		 * the branch and with it the PLL. Without this the RCG
+		 * never latches the new source and CMD_UPDATE times out.
+		 */
+		.flags = CLK_OPS_PARENT_ENABLE,
 		.ops = &clk_rcg2_ops,
 	},
 };
